+# Codex organizer proposal — PRO-09
+
+**Status: proposal; Windows and Discord acceptance are `PENDING-LIVE`.** This
+branch is intended for orchestrator review and integration. There has been no
+successful live end-to-end recording demonstration. Preview capture, four
+concurrent feeds, and the one-click organizer remain targets, not demonstrated
+product capabilities.
+
+## Target interaction
+
+After opening Discord call pop-outs, the operator says:
+
+> Anchor the Discord windows to Café and start recording in folder Demo 01.
+
+The intended sequence is:
+
+1. Codex calls `organizer_status` and checks the selected-root flag and actual
+   encoder-trial readiness. A selected executable alone does not mean ready.
+2. Codex calls `list_discord_windows` and treats every title as untrusted data.
+   Only a window classified `Popout` is eligible. `Unknown` is listed, but never
+   selected for anchoring or recording.
+3. Codex calls `propose_recording_plan` with `folder_name: "Demo 01"` and, when
+   needed, an explicit list of the returned opaque tokens. Omitting tokens means
+   all currently classified pop-outs, within the capsule bound.
+4. Codex tells the operator to inspect the titles and folder segment and click
+   **Confirm inside Café**. MCP cannot confirm, reject, or simulate this click.
+5. Codex polls `plan_result` for that exact `plan_id`. It describes a recording
+   only after that window's actual outcome is `recording`.
+
+A proposal has no capture, capsule, folder-creation, or recording effect. One
+pending proposal is allowed at a time; another yields `plan_pending`. Its
+lifetime is 30 seconds. Rejection and expiry leave no execution authority behind.
+The confirm path re-resolves and compares every frozen window; a changed window
+gets its own closed result instead of being silently substituted.
+The same frozen observation is checked again before an organizer start and
+after slow encoder preparation. A partial anchor failure retains a bounded
+identity-to-capsule reservation so retry cannot silently create another capsule.
+
+Stopping all recordings uses `propose_stop_all` and another native confirmation.
+This is separate from stopping an individual tile through the local operator
+channel. No organizer operation configures FFmpeg, OBS, or Twitch, or sends a
+capsule to OBS.
+
+## Register the proposed server in Codex
+
+The operator must run Codex and Café on the same Windows installation and use
+Café's current, private session broker rendezvous. The rendezvous directory is a
+trusted launch setting, not an MCP argument. Its secret is obtained through the
+existing private rendezvous mechanism and kept in memory. Do not put ticket
+contents in configuration, environment variables, logs, or chat.
+
+The official [Codex MCP configuration documentation](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/extend/mcp?surface=cli)
+describes stdio `command`, `args`, and `cwd` entries under `mcp_servers` in the
+user's Codex configuration, plus `codex mcp list` and `/mcp` for inspection.
+The following is a **synthetic Windows example**, to adapt locally after the
+orchestrator has integrated and gated this branch:
+
+```toml
+[mcp_servers.cafe_organizer]
+command = 'C:\Cafe\Python\python.exe'
+args = ['-B', '-m', 'cafe.mcp_server', '--organizer-rendezvous', 'C:\Cafe\private\session\broker']
+cwd = 'C:\Cafe\source\connectors'
+enabled_tools = ['organizer_status', 'list_discord_windows', 'propose_recording_plan', 'plan_result', 'propose_stop_all']
+startup_timeout_sec = 10
+tool_timeout_sec = 15
+```
+
+`cwd` supplies the Python package's import location. Replace the interpreter,
+source directory, and current session directory using trusted local deployment
+information. These example paths do not identify a user or an actual session.
+The operator must provision that session-location handoff; this proposal does
+not add an Electron launcher or persist session discovery in MCP arguments.
+
+Inspect registration with:
+
+```text
+codex mcp list
+```
+
+In Codex's terminal interface, `/mcp` lists active servers. Successful discovery
+is only a configuration check. The first `organizer_status` must reach the
+running native authority. No provider means the five organizer tools are not
+listed. An explicitly configured but absent or unreachable authority produces
+`unavailable`; it does not create simulated state. A restarted Café session may
+require updating the trusted rendezvous setting and restarting this MCP process.
+
+The existing chat and diagnostics options remain independent. Direct
+`start_recording`, `stop_recording`, and `send_to_obs` MCP tools still require
+their own trusted control provider and confirmation source. This proposal does
+not enable them through the organizer provider.
+
+## Protocol and state contract
+
+| Tool | Input | Proposed result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `organizer_status` | `{}` | `organizer_plan`, `folder_root_set`, `encoder_ready`, `capsule_count`, `recording_count` |
+| `list_discord_windows` | `{}` | `windows` rows with `token`, `title`, `classification`, `bound_capsule` |
+| `propose_recording_plan` | `folder_name`, optional `tokens` | `plan_id`, `state: "pending_confirmation"` |
+| `plan_result` | `plan_id` | Pending, rejected, expired, or completed with per-window outcomes |
+| `propose_stop_all` | Optional `capsule_ids` | A distinct `plan_id`, `state: "pending_confirmation"` |
+
+The remote request body has exactly these top-level fields:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": "cafe.organizer.v1",
+  "kind": "organizer_request",
+  "request_id": "synthetic-request",
+  "authority_epoch": "7",
+  "body": {
+    "op": "propose_recording_plan",
+    "folder_name": "Demo 01"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The transport wraps this in the existing authenticated `control` capability.
+The core routes only the five closed organizer operations to its serialized
+actor. The broker reply binds the request ID and contains `data` and `error`;
+the MCP adapter exposes only validated data or one closed error. It never
+serializes broker tickets, native approval tokens, output paths, or exception
+text. Window identity tokens are opaque selectors returned only in the window
+listing; they are not credentials, executable arguments, or paths.
+
+`organizer_plan` in native state is either `null` or exactly:
+
+```json
+{
+  "plan_id": "organizer-7-1",
+  "windows": [{"title": "Synthetic call"}],
+  "folder_name": "Demo 01",
+  "expires_unix_ms": 946684830000
+}
+```
+
+Expiry is a safe JSON integer in Unix milliseconds. A stop plan uses an empty
+`folder_name`; it does not select a folder. Native state also adds `auto_anchor`
+(default `false`), `recordings[].reason` (closed string or `null`), and
+`preview_sources` rows containing `capsule_id`, `feed_id`, and a
+`window:<decimal>:0` source identifier obtained from the registry's actual
+native handle. Synthetic fixtures do not invent preview source handles.
+Before projection, the native lifetime witness, process identity and observed
+window metadata are rechecked. Bound-window liveness is refreshed independently
+of optional discovery. `feed_availability` marks each current binding available
+or unavailable; closure never deletes the capsule or its recordings. These
+source identifiers are metadata, not evidence that Electron rendered a preview.
+
+`plan_result` uses `state: "pending_confirmation"`, `"rejected"`, or
+`"expired"` with `windows: []`, or `state: "completed"` with terminal rows
+`{title, capsule_id, state}`. The core may be executing already confirmed jobs
+between observations; `plan_result` returns `unavailable` during that interval.
+Poll again or inspect status. Do not infer a failure, repeat confirmation, or
+propose another effect from that transient error. A lost transport response is
+also uncertain; the adapter deliberately does not replay the proposal.
+
+A completed plan can contain a mixture of `recording`, `stopped`, and failures.
+Closed window reasons include `encoder_session_limit`,
+`capture_start_unavailable`, `window_unavailable`, `window_titles_identical`,
+`window_changed`, `folder_not_authorized`, `disk_write_failed`, `capsule_limit`,
+`already_recording`, `encoder_unavailable`, and `unavailable`. A terminal outcome
+is a historical observation, not a promise that the recording remains healthy.
+
+Top-level errors are exactly `folder_root_required`, `folder_name_invalid`,
+`no_discord_windows`, `window_titles_identical`, `plan_pending`, `plan_unknown`,
+and `unavailable`. The folder argument is one ASCII segment matching
+`^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9 _-]{0,63}$`, bounded to 64 characters. Root selection and
+canonical-root/reparse validation belong to the native authority. MCP never
+receives or chooses the full recording path.
+
+The new private operator bodies are documented separately in
+[`organizer_operator_ops.v1.json`](../schemas/organizer_operator_ops.v1.json).
+`organizer_plan_confirm`, `organizer_plan_reject`, and `set_auto_anchor` are not
+valid broker operations, regardless of fields or claims sent by a caller.
+The broker request schema is
+[`organizer_request.v1.json`](../schemas/organizer_request.v1.json).
+
+## Auto-anchor and same-title scope
+
+The proposed auto-anchor loop is enabled only by a trusted local
+`set_auto_anchor` operation. It starts off after every process start, polls no
+more frequently than once per second, labels new capsules `slot-N`, and binds
+role `game` to the observed full-window crop. It does not start recordings.
+Closed sources become unavailable; recordings are not deleted. A changed layout
+may be re-paired only while its capsule has no active recording. No recording
+is restarted implicitly.
+
+The Discord executable allowlist is `Discord.exe`, `DiscordPTB.exe`, and
+`DiscordCanary.exe`. Real class/title patterns have not been measured. The
+single `PENDING_LIVE_DISCORD_PATTERNS` constant is intentionally empty in this
+proposal: allowlisted executables therefore remain `Unknown`. This is an
+explicit live-measurement gate, not an invented Discord heuristic.
+
+The security-owned identity regions and the existing ambiguous-window test
+remain unchanged. The default unique-descriptor resolver rejects ambiguous
+same-title windows with `window_titles_identical` at pairing/start boundaries.
+An optional, isolated last commit can introduce exact-handle/generation capture
+resolution outside those regions. It requires measurement and operator approval
+before integration. OBS retains unique-descriptor resolution.
+
+## Durable action attribution
+
+Capsule creation and pairing use the existing durable `control` envelopes;
+their flushed admission is recorded before the corresponding binding is made
+available. Structural request/event IDs use the `organizer-` namespace because
+that envelope permits only alphanumerics, hyphens and underscores. Its schema
+does not support a separate structural outcome record or a literal `actor`
+field. Folder selection and recording start/stop use distinct ordinary confirmed
+intent/result records with `identity_sha256 = SHA256("organizer")` and the
+`organizer.` request namespace.
+
+Folder creation is preceded by its durable intent. Windows ancestor directory
+handles deny write/delete sharing during creation, and canonical-root/reparse
+validation precedes the result. The selected picker root remains separate from
+the plan's child folder. This does not change the recorder owner's later output
+opening implementation.
+
+These are the concrete attribution fields in this proposal, not a claim of a
+universal actor-bearing journal. Plan rejection, expiry and the default-off
+auto-anchor toggle remain in-memory administrative transitions. If the required
+"every action" contract includes those transitions and explicit structural
+outcomes, the journal owner must extend schema/replay outside this branch's
+write list before that contract is complete.
+
+## Remaining integration and live gates
+
+- **Native confirmation UI — `PENDING-LIVE`:** this branch is scoped to core and
+  MCP. The Electron owner must expose the pending plan and send confirm/reject
+  through its trusted private operator channel. This branch does not modify
+  `ui/` or `src/`, and no MCP fallback substitutes for that work.
+- **Host state projection — `PENDING-LIVE`:** the existing host parser's
+  `maxLineBytes` is 4096, and the core snapshot falls back above 3500 bytes.
+  The draft preserves that fail-closed behavior. Twelve full capsule states and
+  the new frozen fields require the host/UI owner to extend framing bounds and
+  validators. A core state field alone is not evidence that the UI renders it.
+  The broker has a separate bounded response budget; an oversized window list
+  returns `unavailable` instead of a misleading partial catalogue.
+- **Capture and previews — `PENDING-LIVE`:** validate actual native handles,
+  Discord pop-out patterns, lifecycle changes, preview capture, first frames,
+  consent boundaries, and recovery on Windows.
+- **Concurrent recording — `[TARGET]` at least four feeds, `PENDING-LIVE`:**
+  hardware session capacity is unknown. A successful hardware trial indicates
+  readiness for the selected approval, not availability of another concurrent
+  session. There is no software-encoder fallback. Slow native startup may delay
+  operator input despite ticking existing feeds during asynchronous preparation;
+  local input is revisited between setup jobs rather than after a whole batch.
+  interruptible native startup is a separate runtime-owner integration gate.
+- **Full trial reuse remains an owner dependency:** `ffmpeg_recorder.rs` keeps a
+  private, non-Clone `Preflight` consumed by `start_ready`. The allowed resource
+  patch sizes pools from observed geometry and caches the successful hardware
+  encoder preference, but still re-trials each feed. Reusing an approved trial
+  needs a recorder-owner API that revalidates approval and produces a fresh
+  geometry-bound preflight. No such capability is forged or claimed here.
+- **Publication:** all draft commits use `[skip ci]`; this proposal starts no
+  hosted CI, opens no PR, and is not a release. New tracked files may require
+  the integration owner to rebuild the existing router index.
+
+## Synthetic checks
+
+These checks exercise input/refusal contracts, provider discovery, explicit
+MCP registration arguments, real authenticated framing over a synthetic local
+peer, and per-plan outcome projection. They do not enumerate Discord, click the
+native UI, or create real media:
+
+```text
+python -m unittest discover -s tests/integration -p test_mcp_organizer.py -v
+python -m unittest discover -s tests/integration -p test_mcp_control*.py -v
+python -m unittest discover -s tests/integration -p test_mcp_server.py -v
+```
+
+Run socket transport checks where local socket I/O is permitted. A sandbox
+transport restriction must be reported as such, not counted as Windows
+acceptance or converted to a fake provider success.
+
+### Reproduce the four-feed failure-isolation scenario
+
+`core/tests/organizer.rs` contains `assert_four_feed_failure_isolation`.
+The existing recorder fixture starts its current executable with an exact root
+fixture name. The production main file may change only module declarations,
+and adding a Cargo test target is outside this branch's dependency/manifest
+scope. The standalone harness below supplies that root fixture and calls the
+committed scenario. It uses the repository's compiled, locked dependencies;
+it does not edit a manifest or substitute an encoder capability.
+
+Save this complete stdlib script in a scratch directory outside the checkout,
+then run it from the repository root after `cargo test --locked --no-run` has
+compiled the dependencies. A synthetic Windows invocation is:
+
+```text
+python C:\Cafe\scratch\verify_four_feeds.py
+```
+
+Expected result: exactly the named four-feed test passes. It creates four
+independent synthetic recorder children, closes one synthetic source, and
+checks that the remaining three stay active. This is **not** evidence of four
+native Discord captures, hardware encoder sessions, or published media.
+
+```python
+"""Run the committed four-feed scenario with the recorder's required root fixture.
+
+Run from the repository root after compiling its locked Cargo dependencies.
+This is a synthetic Rust child/pipe check, not Windows capture evidence.
+"""
+import json
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+import subprocess
+import sys
+import tempfile
+
+repo = Path.cwd().resolve()
+deps = repo / "target" / "debug" / "deps"
+modules = [
+    "capsule_registry", "authority_journal", "journal_replay", "capsule_pairing",
+    "capture_frame_pool", "capture_health", "capture_pipeline", "recorder_pacer",
+    "ffmpeg_recorder", "windows_window_registry", "windows_graphics_capture",
+    "runtime_effects", "runtime_recording", "discord_windows", "organizer",
+]
+source = ["#![allow(dead_code)]"]
+for module in modules:
+    path = (repo / "core" / "src" / (module + ".rs")).as_posix()
+    source.append(f"#[path = {json.dumps(path)}] mod {module};")
+windows_path = (repo / "core" / "src" / "windows_journal_policy.rs").as_posix()
+source.append(f"#[cfg(windows)] #[path = {json.dumps(windows_path)}] mod windows_journal_policy;")
+test_path = (repo / "core" / "tests" / "organizer.rs").as_posix()
+source.append(f"#[path = {json.dumps(test_path)}] mod organizer_contract_tests;")
+source.append(r'''
+#[test]
+fn recorder_child_fixture() {
+    if let Ok(mode) = std::env::var("CAFE_RECORDER_FIXTURE_MODE") {
+        match mode.as_str() {
+            "drain" => { std::io::copy(&mut std::io::stdin(), &mut std::io::sink()).unwrap(); },
+            _ => std::process::exit(23),
+        }
+    }
+}
+#[test]
+fn four_concurrent_synthetic_feeds_keep_three_running_after_one_closes() {
+    organizer_contract_tests::assert_four_feed_failure_isolation();
+}
+''')
+with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cafe-organizer-check-") as scratch:
+    root = Path(scratch)
+    harness = root / "synthetic_feeds.rs"
+    executable = root / ("synthetic_feeds.exe" if os.name == "nt" else "synthetic_feeds")
+    harness.write_text("\n".join(source), encoding="utf-8")
+    command = ["rustc", "--edition=2024", "--test", str(harness),
+               "-L", "dependency=" + str(deps), "-o", str(executable)]
+    externs = ["serde", "serde_json", "sha2", "tokio"]
+    if os.name == "nt":
+        externs.append("windows")
+    for name in externs:
+        candidates = list(deps.glob("lib" + name + "-*.rlib"))
+        if not candidates:
+            raise SystemExit("Missing compiled dependency: " + name)
+        artifact = max(candidates, key=lambda path: path.stat().st_mtime_ns)
+        command.extend(["--extern", name + "=" + str(artifact)])
+    subprocess.run(command, check=True)
+    arguments = sys.argv[1:] or ["--exact",
+        "four_concurrent_synthetic_feeds_keep_three_running_after_one_closes", "--nocapture"]
+    subprocess.run([str(executable), *arguments], check=True)
+```
